    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25xjkSizeFBrzHTULVxNtCU)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main` (after #523, #524); independent of the other open PRs.\n- Only touches `tests/sp-agenda-views-inline-test.el` and a bullet in `sp-org-agenda.org`.\n\n## What I found\n\n- The test file did not load: `invalid-read-syntax \")\" 25 66`. One closing paren too many at the end of the loader `let` (it came from #395 and was never run, because I had no Emacs).\n- The old `entry-key` test would also have failed once it loaded: it called `org-agenda-files`, which the test does not define.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed the extra paren.\n- `entry-key` now stubs `sp-agenda-views-inline-files`.\n- A bullet in the module's \"Changes by pull request\" list.\n- `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Checked by Claude\n\n- Installed Emacs 29.3 this time: `check-parens` passes on the test file and on `sp-agenda-views.el`.\n- `emacs -Q --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-agenda-views-inline-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit`: 9 of 9 pass (including the filter and SOURCEREFS tests from #523).\n- CI's tangle check already passed on #523, so the `.el` and `.org` code match.\n- Not run: the interactive commands and the transient menu in a GUI Emacs (and Emacs 31).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `emacs -Q --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-agenda-views-inline-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes on your Emacs\n- [x] `C-c o X`, `f`, pick `SOURCEREFS`: the view lists only SOURCEREFS entries\n- [x] `C-c o X`, `c`: all keywords again\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9taQEBJAWpQmkyfLY)_",
